cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "odesuite: a from-scratch ODE solver library and learning studio"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ediz
    email: ce298.dynamics@gmail.com
# repository-code: add this once the project has a public home. There is no
# remote configured, and a guessed URL in a citation file is worse than none.
abstract: >-
  A from-scratch ordinary differential equation solver library — adaptive
  Runge-Kutta pairs, Radau IIA and Rosenbrock stiff solvers, symplectic and
  exponential integrators, arbitrary-order Taylor series by jet arithmetic,
  dense output, event location, mass matrices and index-1 DAEs, boundary value
  problems by multiple shooting, and forward parameter sensitivities — together
  with a desktop application that teaches a first course in differential
  equations over it.
keywords:
  - ordinary differential equations
  - numerical analysis
  - Runge-Kutta
  - stiff solvers
  - differential-algebraic equations
  - mathematics education
license: MIT
version: 0.4.0
